# sem-step — UX design sheet prompt
# One display-mode sheet for the sem-step child element: its mode axis is
# the status vocabulary (done | current | todo default | blocked), staged
# as one example pane per mode at desktop width, plus the same vocabulary
# at narrow mobile width where wrapped prose must never orphan a status
# glyph. Dark minimal-tech page hosting light documentation panes, as the
# reference site's example viewer stages them. Reference attachments are
# the judged renders from the snap harness (see reports/tag-sem-step.md).

schema: "0.4"
id: sem-step-ux-sheet
type: image
quality: high

prompt:
  text: |
    A precise UX design sheet for the SemText vocabulary element
    `sem-step` (a CSS-only, status-annotated instruction step inside a
    procedure — zero JavaScript), rendered as FOUR example panes on a
    dark minimal-tech canvas (page background #0f172a) whose light
    documentation panes (card surface #f8fafc, hairline borders
    #e2e8f0) each hold one step in one lifecycle mode. Status colours:
    green success #34d399, blue current #60a5fa, muted grey todo
    #94a3b8, red blocked #f87171.

    PANE 1 — DONE mode. One step card: thin solid green rail at its
    left edge, positional ordinal (1) in a separate narrow muted gutter
    column — a CSS-counter, never part of the step text — prose in the
    foreground, and a small green check glyph " ✓" trailing the last
    word, glued to it on the same line.

    PANE 2 — CURRENT mode. Same anatomy: solid blue rail, ordinal 2, a
    small blue arrow glyph " →" trailing the text, the row quietly
    signalling "in progress now" without any animation.

    PANE 3 — TODO mode, shown twice side by side to prove the spellings
    are equivalent: a step with an explicit todo status and a step
    carrying no attribute at all. Both render identically — muted grey
    DASHED rail (dashes, not solid), ordinal 3/4, small grey ring glyph
    " ○" trailing the text. The prose stays fully dark and legible;
    only the rail and glyph are muted. Unstarted must read as visibly
    pending, never as missing or hidden.

    PANE 4 — BLOCKED mode at narrow mobile width (390 px). Red solid
    rail, ordinal 5, muted red-tinted body text that still reads fully,
    a small red no-entry glyph " ⛔" trailing the last word. Give this
    step a long instruction so the prose wraps to three lines: the
    glyph must stay attached to the final word on the last line, never
    dropped alone onto a line of its own. The other panes may also show
    their trailing glyph inline with wrapped text under the same rule.

    Typography: clean humanist sans for step prose, tabular ordinals in
    the gutter, no monospace anywhere (no code inside the panes). Flat,
    engineered, restrained — a documentation specimen, not an
    illustration. Rails, ordinals and glyphs are quiet furniture; the
    reader's eye lands on which step is done, running, pending or
    blocked at a glance.
  negative: |
    no status glyph (✓, →, ○, ⛔) sitting alone on its own line away
    from its step text, no hidden or dropped todo step (unstarted is
    visible, just muted), no hand-typed step numbers inside the prose,
    no ordinal rendered inline with the text, no visible kind badge or
    label, no buttons, checkboxes, collapse arrows or any
    interactive-looking control (the element is static), no solid blocks
    occluding words, no decorative photos or glow, no watermarks, no
    browser chrome, no light-mode page canvas, no solid todo rail
    (todo's rail is dashed).
  style: flat dark technical documentation specimen with light content panes, minimal-tech design system

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-step-fixture/sem-step-status-vocabulary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-step-fixture/sem-step-status-vocabulary-render-390.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-step-fixture/sem-step-class-form-render-390.png
    role: reference

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-step-ux-sheet.png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024

requirements:
  pages:
    - name: done-current-todo-blocked-sheet
      must_show:
        - ordinal in a separate muted gutter column per step, never inside the prose
        - status rail per mode: green solid (done), blue solid (current), grey DASHED (todo, both spellings), red solid (blocked)
        - trailing status glyph glued to the step's last word in every mode
        - todo shown twice (explicit status and no attribute) rendering identically
        - blocked prose muted but fully readable, glyph still attached after wrapping
      must_never:
        - orphan a status glyph onto its own line
        - render a todo step with a solid rail or hide it entirely
        - show interactive controls, badges, or hand-typed ordinals in prose

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
    criteria:
      mode-legibility:
        weight: 0.3
        description: all four lifecycle modes read distinctly at a glance; todo is visibly pending, not missing
        fail_signals:
          - todo row looks identical to an unstyled paragraph with no rail or glyph
          - two modes render the same rail and glyph
      glyph-attachment:
        weight: 0.3
        description: every trailing glyph sits on the same line as the step's last word, including across wrapped prose
        fail_signals:
          - a glyph alone on its own line
          - a glyph separated from its text by a visible gap the width of a word
      gutter-anatomy:
        weight: 0.2
        description: ordinal, rail and prose occupy separate visual channels with even rhythm
        fail_signals:
          - ordinals inside the prose text
          - rails touching or crossing the prose column
      specimen-restraint:
        weight: 0.2
        description: flat documentation look on the dark canvas, no illustration drift
        fail_signals:
          - decorative imagery, glow or gradients on the panes
          - visible buttons or controls
    reject_if:
      - any status glyph is orphaned on its own line
      - the todo step is missing, hidden, or rendered with a solid rail
      - the blocked step's text is illegible or occluded
